    title: 'Expedition Dinosaur',
    description:
      'Travel back in time with Expedition: Dinosaur! It’s the most fun you’ve had in the last 75 million years! Coming to Science Spectrum February 15th through June 1st, 2025!\n\nThis exhibition combines engaging interactives with life-like animatronic dinosaurs and exciting educational content. These realistic robotic creatures will awe guests with their lifelike size, thrilling sounds, and exciting special effects. Visitors will feel as if they are truly walking among the dinosaurs. \n\nDiscover more about these dynamic Jurassic dinosaur species:\n●\tAlbertosaurus (Related to Tyrannosaurus Rex)\n●\tAmargasaurus\n●\tCarnotaurus\n●\tKentrosaurus\n●\tPachycephalosaurus\n●\tVelociraptors\n●\tDilophosaurus\n●\tTriceratops\n●\tStegosaurus\n\nIn addition to the amazing animatronics, Expedition: Dinosaur incorporates a wide range of hands-on interactive experiences into the exhibit. Step into the shoes of a paleontologist with interactive cabinets filled with excavation artifacts and fossils. Guests of all ages can also play around with the augmented reality sandbox to learn how Earth’s climate is affected by the landscape. Try your hand at the egg incubator robot, but be careful not to crack under pressure! Solve puzzles that allow guests to mix and match dinosaur species and put together Pangea from our contemporary continents. Children can also stop by the rubbing station to take home an etching of several species of dinosaur. \n\nThere are also several interactives focused on the anatomy of dinosaurs. Guests can see the movement of dinosaurs’ tails, the function of dinosaur gizzards, the process of dinosaur eggs hatching, and a simulation of dinosaurs knocking heads. \n\nAfter visiting the Jurassic era, guests will not only take away the awe of seeing these beautiful creatures and fascinating facts about the prehistoric landscape but the exhibit also features an extraordinary photo-op with a T-Rex head for a very unique souvenir!\n\nAdditionally, the OMNI Theater will be offering a limited run of the film, Dinosaurs: Giants of Patagonia. This film will be available in the OMNI Theater starting February 14th until June 1st. Showtimes, trailer and ticket pricing can be found on our website:https://www.sciencespectrum.org\nThis exhibition will be located in the Exhibit Hall at the Science Spectrum, and will be open during regular museum hours.\n\nExpedition: Dinosaur Pricing:\nGeneral Admission: \tExhibit w/Museum OR Film\tExhibit w/ Museum & Film\nAdult\t\t\t           $14.50\t\t\t           $20.00\nChild & Senior\t\t$12.00\t\t\t\t$17.00\n\n**Special rates available for groups and members**\n**30 minute guided tours are available with large or school group reservations**\n\nExpedition Dinosaur® was created by Stage Nine Design and is distributed by Exhibits Development Group.\n',
