    id: 'f934cb92-6b35-1b5c-450b-6acaf04b8af9',
    name: "h2c2's 48 Hour Film Festival",
    title: "h2c2's 48 Hour Film Festival",
    description:
      "Are you a seasoned film maker, or have you ever wanted to try your hand at making one? Now's your chance! h2c2 is hosting it's first ever 48 Hour Film Festival! 48HFF is a high-energy, fast-paced creative exercise where filmmaking teams are challenged to write, shoot, edit, and deliver a short film—all within just 48 hours. At the Friday, May 23rd, kick off, each team will learn what elements are required for their film so teams cannot work on their films outside of the 48 hour time limit. Completed films are due by Sunday, May 25th at 8pm. There will be $5 showings of the films from May 28th-31st with the opportunity for audience members to vote on their favorite films. \n\nTeam registration fees are $10 per team (not individual). Teams can have up to 12 members. Solo film makers are also welcome to sign up as a team of one. The sign up form can be found in our Google Drive folder, along with festival rules and resources. https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/103Apz_WrLXmIPx4be9nEibNFmx9gT-iv?usp=drive_link \n\nHave more questions? For more information, email h2c2lubbock@gmail.com. \n\nWe are so excited to see the new works that get made in Lubbock at our first 48HFF!",
